I have a few questions before I implement this.

1. Command name and ID?
   - a) `convo.complete-apply`, "Convo: Complete and Apply"
   - b) `convo.complete-apply-all`, "Convo: Complete and Apply All"
   - c) Something else (please specify)

2. Keybinding?
   - a) None
   - b) `Ctrl+Alt+R` / `Cmd+Alt+R`
   - c) Something else (please specify)

3. Should it also appear as a button in the editor title bar of `.convo` files?
   - a) Yes, with a `$(rocket)` icon
   - b) Yes, with a different icon (please specify)
   - c) No, Command Palette only

4. Which blocks should be applied after the completion finishes?
   - a) Only blocks in messages added by this completion. This includes multiple assistant messages if function calls happen.
   - b) Only blocks in the last assistant message
   - c) Blocks in the last message group that has blocks, the same as the last group in the Code Blocks view

5. You mentioned file blocks, and the notification mentions bash scripts. Should `RUNNABLE_SCRIPT` blocks also run?
   - a) Yes. Write files and run scripts in the order they appear, the same way `Apply All` works now
   - b) Yes, but write all files first and then run scripts
   - c) No, only write file blocks. I will drop the script part from the notification text.

6. Confirmation behavior, since the progress notification already gives a warning:
   - a) No confirmation. Write files and run scripts automatically, ignoring `convo.alwaysRunOutputScripts`.
   - b) Write files automatically, but still ask before running scripts unless `convo.alwaysRunOutputScripts` is true
   - c) Show one confirmation modal before applying, like `Apply All`

7. Progress notification text. Something like this:
   - a) Title `Completing conversation`, message `<path> · File blocks will be written and scripts will be executed automatically`
   - b) Title `Completing and applying`, with the same message as a)
   - c) Custom wording (please specify)

8. If the completion fails or is cancelled, nothing will be applied. If a find-replace target isn't found, what should happen?
   - a) Show the existing error and continue applying the other blocks
   - b) Stop and apply nothing more

9. Implementation placement. `completeAsync` lives inside `registerCompletionCommands`. Which approach do you prefer?
   - a) Add a new `complete-apply.ts` with `registerCompleteApplyCommand`. Add an `onComplete` callback and a `progressMessage` option to `CompletionOptions`, and have the new file call `convo.complete` through an internal command that accepts those options.
   - b) Extract `completeAsync` into its own exported module so `complete-apply.ts` can call it directly. This is a larger refactor.


